- Story & Context: Weeks after the monastery was evacuated by local authorities, squatter-artist Sister Clara returned through the salt marshes to find the priory’s sanctum scorched black and smelling of ionized copper. The Eurorack synthesizers were still humming in self-generating drone cycles, triggered by an autonomous mechanical pendulum that ceaselessly tapped out erratic rhythms against a solitary bongo skin while a prerecorded tape looped into the empty choir: "The storm took the choir but spared the patchcord." Her field recording of that supernatural residue closes the record, letting the bone-dry bongo gallop dissolve into shivering, ghostly radio drift.
